   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 460 of the laws of 2021 amending the vehicle and\ntraffic law, the general municipal law and the public officers law relating to\ncertain traffic infractions and notices of liability and amending the vehicle\nand traffic law relating to adjudications and owner liability for a violation\nof traffic-control signal indications in the village of Pelham Manor, in\nrelation to the effectiveness thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S9639",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S9639-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §14, Chap 460 of 2021",
    "lawSection": "Vehicle and Traffic",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S9639\n\nSPONSOR: FERNANDEZ\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 460 of the laws of 2021 amending the vehicle and\ntraffic law, the general municipal law and the public officers law\nrelating to certain traffic infractions and notices of liability and\namending the vehicle and traffic law relating to adjudications and owner\nliability for a violation of traffic-control signal indications in the\nvillage of Pelham Manor, in relation to the effectiveness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo extend the expiration of the red-light camera program in the village\nof Pelham Manor.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one of this bill amends section 14 of chapter 460 of the laws of\n2021 to extend the expiration of the authorization for traffic-control\nsignal photo violation monitoring devices from December 1, 2026, to\nDecember 1, 2031.\n\nSection two provides the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill extends the sunset provision of the 2021 law authorizing the\nvillage of Pelham Manor to install and operate traffic- control signal\nphoto violation-monitoring devices or \"red light cameras.\" The extension\nensures continuity of enforcement of traffic-control signal violations\nand supports public safety objectives by allowing the program to contin-\nue through December 1, 2031.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediate.\n",
